# Everything in here ends up on a Linux router or in a Linux build, so
# everything is stored and checked out with LF - including on Windows.
#
# A CRLF checkout of a shell script makes the kernel report
#
#     bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M
#
# and nothing starts. The blanket rule below is deliberate: the per-extension
# rules that used to be here covered the service scripts and missed the web
# interface and the tests, which is exactly the sort of gap that only shows up
# once somebody has edited a file on the wrong machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...except the things that are not text at all and must never be touched by
# any filter.
prebuilt/**       binary
*.png             binary
*.dat             binary
*.ipk             binary
*.apk             binary
